(Every date export, called the way you would actually use it: a fixed
 moment taken apart into its civil fields, moved around the calendar,
 written out in every documented layout, and read back in from the forms
 a person or a log file would actually hand you.

 This demo is the library's test - its output is compared byte for byte
 against date_demo.expected - so everything after the first section uses
 the one fixed moment throughout, rather than 'the moment now', so the
 transcript is the same every time it runs.

   vox date.vox --shared -o libdate.so
   vox date_demo.vox --link date -o date_demo
   ./date_demo)

see date version "0.1" from "./libdate.lib".

(--- Now ---)
Print "--- now ---".
a number called 'right now' is 'the moment now'.
a boolean called 'the year has reached 2026' is false.
If {'the year of' of 'right now'} is greater than or equal to 2026 then, set 'the year has reached 2026' to true.
Print "'the moment now' is a number of seconds since 1970, and the year it names has reached 2026: {'the year has reached 2026'}".

(--- Civil time to a moment, and back ---)
Print "--- civil time to a moment ---".
a number called 'the moment of a birthday' is 'the moment of' with 2026 and 7 and 29.
Print "'the moment of' 2026-07-29 is the number {'the moment of a birthday'}".
a number called 'the same moment with a clock time' is 'the moment at' with 2026 and 7 and 29 and 16 and 2 and 48.
Print "'the moment at' 2026-07-29 16:02:48 is {'the same moment with a clock time'}".
(Fields that overflow normalise rather than refuse: day 32 of January is 1 February.)
a number called 'day 32 of january' is 'the moment of' with 2026 and 1 and 32.
a number called 'the 1st of february' is 'the moment of' with 2026 and 2 and 1.
a boolean called 'the overflow normalised correctly' is false.
If 'day 32 of january' is 'the 1st of february' then, set 'the overflow normalised correctly' to true.
Print "day 32 of january normalises to 1 february: {'the overflow normalised correctly'}".

(--- A moment to its parts ---)
Print "--- a moment to its parts ---".
a number called moment is 'the same moment with a clock time'.
Print "year {'the year of' of moment}, month {'the month of' of moment}, day {'the day of month of' of moment}".
Print "hour {'the hour of' of moment}, minute {'the minute of' of moment}, second {'the second of' of moment}".
Print "weekday {'the weekday of' of moment} (1 Monday .. 7 Sunday), day of year {'the day of year of' of moment}".
Print "iso week {'the iso week of' of moment} of iso year {'the iso week year of' of moment}".
Print "quarter {'the quarter of' of moment}, century {'the century of' of moment}".

(--- Names ---)
Print "--- names ---".
Print "month 7 is {'the month name of' of 7}, or {'the short month name of' of 7} for short".
Print "weekday 3 is {'the weekday name of' of 3}, or {'the short weekday name of' of 3} for short".
Print "a month outside 1..12 has no name: [{'the month name of' of 0}]".

(--- Calendar facts ---)
Print "--- calendar facts ---".
Print "2024 is a leap year: {'is a leap year' of 2024}, and 2023 is: {'is a leap year' of 2023}".
Print "february 2024 has {'the days in' of 2 and 2024} days; february 2023 has {'the days in' of 2 and 2023}".
Print "29 february 2024 is a valid date: {'is a valid date' of 2024 and 2 and 29}, 29 february 2023 is: {'is a valid date' of 2023 and 2 and 29}".
Print "24:00:00 is a valid time: {'is a valid time' of 24 and 0 and 0}".

(--- Moving around the calendar ---)
Print "--- moving around the calendar ---".
a text called 'the layout for a plain date' is "%F".
a number called 'a week later' is 'weeks later' of moment and 1.
Print "a week later: {'the moment written as' of 'a week later' and 'the layout for a plain date'}".
(The documented departure from GNU: a month later clamps the day of
 month rather than overflowing into the month after.)
a number called 'the 31st of january' is 'the moment of' with 2026 and 1 and 31.
a number called 'the 31st of january plus one month' is 'months later' of 'the 31st of january' and 1.
Print "31 january plus one month clamps to: {'the moment written as' of 'the 31st of january plus one month' and 'the layout for a plain date'}".
a text called 'the layout for a date and time' is "%F %T".
a number called 'the start of the day' is 'the start of the day of' of moment.
Print "start of the day: {'the moment written as' of 'the start of the day' and 'the layout for a date and time'}".
a number called 'the start of the week' is 'the start of the week of' of moment.
Print "start of the week (monday on or before): {'the moment written as' of 'the start of the week' and 'the layout for a plain date'}".
a number called 'the next monday' is 'the weekday on or after' of moment and 1.
Print "the next monday on or after: {'the moment written as' of 'the next monday' and 'the layout for a plain date'}".
a number called 'new year' is 'the moment of' with 2026 and 1 and 1.
Print "days between new year and this moment: {'the days between' of 'new year' and moment}".

(--- Writing a moment out ---)
Print "--- writing a moment out ---".
a text called 'a full layout' is "%A, %-d %B %Y at %H:%M".
Print "any layout: {'the moment written as' of moment and 'a full layout'}".
Print "'the date of': {'the date of' of moment}".
Print "'the date and time of': {'the date and time of' of moment}".
Print "'the rfc 3339 date and time of': {'the rfc 3339 date and time of' of moment}".
Print "'the rfc email date of': {'the rfc email date of' of moment}".
Print "'the moment in words of': {'the moment in words of' of moment}".

(--- Reading a moment in ---)
Print "--- reading a moment in ---".
a text called 'an iso date' is "2026-07-29".
a number called 'read from an iso date' is 'the moment read from' of 'an iso date'.
Print "'2026-07-29' reads as {'the moment written as' of 'read from an iso date' and 'the layout for a plain date'}".
a text called 'a compact form' is "20260729T160248".
a number called 'read from a compact form' is 'the moment read from' of 'a compact form'.
Print "'20260729T160248' reads as {'the moment written as' of 'read from a compact form' and 'the layout for a date and time'}".
a text called 'a human date' is "29 July 2026".
a number called 'read from a human date' is 'the moment read from' of 'a human date'.
Print "'29 July 2026' reads as {'the moment written as' of 'read from a human date' and 'the layout for a plain date'}".
a text called 'a date that does not exist' is "2026-02-30".
a boolean called 'the impossible date reads as a moment' is 'reads as a moment' of 'a date that does not exist'.
Print "'2026-02-30' does not exist, and reads as a moment: {'the impossible date reads as a moment'}".
a text called garbage is "not a date".
a boolean called 'garbage reads as a moment' is 'reads as a moment' of garbage.
a number called 'garbage read anyway' is 'the moment read from' of garbage.
Print "garbage reads as a moment: {'garbage reads as a moment'}, and reading it anyway gives: {'garbage read anyway'}".

(--- Relative descriptions ---)
Print "--- relative descriptions ---".
a text called 'a layout naming the weekday' is "%A %F".
a number called 'a base moment' is 'the moment of' with 2026 and 9 and 27.
Print "the base moment is {'the moment written as' of 'a base moment' and 'a layout naming the weekday'}".
a text called 'three weeks ago as text' is "3 weeks ago".
a number called 'three weeks ago' is 'the moment described by' of 'three weeks ago as text' and 'a base moment'.
Print "'3 weeks ago' from there is {'the moment written as' of 'three weeks ago' and 'the layout for a plain date'}".
a text called 'next wednesday as text' is "next wednesday".
a number called 'the next wednesday' is 'the moment described by' of 'next wednesday as text' and 'a base moment'.
Print "'next wednesday' from there is {'the moment written as' of 'the next wednesday' and 'the layout for a plain date'}".
a text called 'an absolute description' is "2026-01-01 + 7 days".
a number called 'an absolute date plus a week' is 'the moment described by' of 'an absolute description' and 'a base moment'.
Print "'2026-01-01 + 7 days' is {'the moment written as' of 'an absolute date plus a week' and 'the layout for a plain date'}, ignoring the base entirely since it names its own absolute moment".
a boolean called 'next wednesday reads as a description' is 'reads as a description' of 'next wednesday as text'.
Print "'next wednesday' reads as a description: {'next wednesday reads as a description'}".
a text called 'not a description' is "not a description at all".
a boolean called 'garbage reads as a description' is 'reads as a description' of 'not a description'.
Print "garbage reads as a description: {'garbage reads as a description'}".
